fp8/*.txt (the e4m3 and e5m2 samples: 24 vectors each of an RTX 1000 Ada, a B200 and, f16 accumulator, an H100: the first 24 of each file, same source commit, same conversion) and
fp8-wgmma/*.txt (the e4m3 and e5m2 f32-accumulator samples: 24 vectors each of an H100 and an H200, recorded through wgmma with a zero accumulator: the first 24 of each file, same source commit, same conversion) and
khattak_sample files (A100.*.txt, H100.*.txt, B200.*.txt, V100.*.txt): 24 test vectors each, copied from the model_validation/ directory of
https://github.com/north-numerical-computing/MATLAB-tensor-core (commit 79143bd29a4a71dc7c2ed47741b63572498b17f6), converted by
tools/tcpapers/khattak_convert.py to one line a vector. They are the recorded results of A100, H100 and B200 cards; the full sets
are 5,000 vectors a file (tools/tcpapers/khattak-fetch.sh downloads them). Which 24: for the A100 files the first 24; for H100 and
B200 the first 8 vectors an RTX 3060 reproduces and the first 16 it does not (so the sample can tell an Ampere sum from a Hopper one); for V100.fp16.fp32.txt
(K = 4, m8n8k4) the first 8 vectors the Ampere rule reproduces and the first 16 it does not (it tells grid 25 from the Volta grid 24), for V100.fp16.fp16.txt the first 24.

